s the Red Death itself, drenched in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask, terrifying the guests and provoking the prince’s rage; when Prospero pursues the figure with a dagger through all seven rooms, the figure turns in the black chamber, and Prospero collapses dead—revealing the figure to be an empty shell, as the plague has infiltrated even the most fortified sanctuary, claiming every life as the lights fade and darkness claims all.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 3,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"is_narrator\": false,\n      \"narrative_role\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_mummer_e8d085c7\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the mummer\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 3,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"is_narrator\": false,\n      \"narrative_role\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pronunciations\": [\n    {\n      \"word\": \"the\",\n      \"flag_reason\": \"proper_noun\",\n      \"occurrences\": 263,\n      \"first_position\": 1,\n      \"chapter_indices\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"﻿The Masque of the Red Death by Edgar Allan Poe (published 1850) THE \\\"Red Death\\\" had long devastated t...\",\n        \"﻿The Masque of the Red Death by Edgar Allan Poe (published 1850) THE \\\"Red Death